    {
      "index": 2,
      "topicId": "64c0e8766f5bfc7ab78aee71",
      "title": "Adsorption isotherms",
      "totalQuestions": 4,
      "questions": [
        {
          "_id": "64c0e8246f5bfc7ab78aeaf5",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "64c0e679aef333185c6bb44c",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2021-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2021",
              "title": "BITSAT 2021"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "Adsorption of a gas follows Freundlich adsorption isotherm. $x$ is the mass of the gas adsorbed on mass $m$ of the adsorbent. The plot of $\\frac{x}{m}$ versus $\\log p$ is shown in the given graph.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/ZhUCvdIYQVA6OhsEZtwkp47cgQrhbfXqZ9TzF793gCw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\frac{x}{m}$ is proportional to :",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "gYNTJ",
              "text": "$p^{2 / 3}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "eQ1jF",
              "text": "$p^{3 / 2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "gnuv1",
              "text": "$p^{3}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "hysx8",
              "text": "$p^{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "According to Freundlich adsorption isotherm $\\frac{x}{m} \\propto p^{\\frac{1}{n}}, \\frac{x}{m}=k p^{\\frac{1}{n}}$\r\n\r\nSlope $=\\frac{2}{3}$\r\n\r\n$\\log \\frac{x}{m}=\\log k+\\frac{1}{n} \\log p$\r\n\r\nSlope $=\\frac{1}{n}=\\frac{2}{3}$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{x}{m} \\propto p^{\\frac{2}{3}}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
          "previousYear": {
            "_id": "64c0e679aef333185c6bb44c",
            "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
            "heldOn": "2021-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
            "isVisible": true,
            "shortName": "2021",
            "title": "BITSAT 2021"
          },
          "evalStatus": "notAttempted",
          "lastPracticed": null
        },
        {
          "_id": "64c0e8096f5bfc7ab78aea04",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7d",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2019-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2019",
              "title": "BITSAT 2019"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "In Freundlich adsorption isotherm, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "YLfYX",
              "text": "between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> in all cases",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "JVyhO",
              "text": "between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> in all cases",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "v9z0N",
              "text": "always <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> in case of physical adsorption",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "HehUV",
              "text": "always <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> in use of chemical adsorption",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Freundlich isotherm is related with the pressure of gas adsorbed, as follows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo></math> amount of gas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></math> adsorbed over the surface of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo></math> pressure of gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo></math> freundlich constant</p><p>Thus, value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>'</mo></math> is always greater than 1 and therefore value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> lies between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
