          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "Which of the following graph is correctly represented according to Freundlich isotherm.",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "v5tpS",
              "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/86555781-f85b-41b4-b7cf-e9a2fc740a1b-image.png\" style=\"width: 168px; height: 170px;\" /></p>",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "D3Yzz",
              "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/0542279d-c55a-4bda-8c3f-a6014639f9ff-8bf60993-dff5-40ca-93b9-4eda26435630-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 185px;\" /></p>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "jB1rh",
              "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/016ebcfc-f596-4750-880c-df5b60ec2790-image.png\" style=\"width: 168px; height: 170px;\" /></p>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "X1RK2",
              "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/0251b59c-646c-4eb5-ac1d-5d232127fad1-image.png\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 170px;\" /></p>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>According to Freundlich adsorption isotherm,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></msup></math><br />where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo></math> mass of gas adsorbed on mass &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&#39; of the absorbent at pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constants.</p><p>Taking logarithm on both sides, we get<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>logx</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>logk</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mi>logp</mi></math></p><p>This is equation of a straight line with slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math> and intercept of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>logk</mi></math>.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
