          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "Which of the following will be the most effective in the coagulation of $\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ soil?",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "UGTTk",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Mg}_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_{4}\\right)_{2}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "BoW4O",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "0RmtH",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{NaCl}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "mOSON",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{KCN}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "According to Hardy-Schulze rule, coagulation power of ions is directly proportional to charge on ion. $\\because \\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ is positively charged colloid. $\\therefore$ It will be coagulated by anion.\r\n(a) $\\mathrm{Mg}_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_{4}\\right)_{2} \\rightleftharpoons 3 \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{PO}_{4}^{3-}$\r\n(b) $\\mathrm{BaCl}_{2} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$\r\n(c) $\\mathrm{NaCl} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Na}^{+}+\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$\r\n(d) $\\mathrm{KCN} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{K}^{+}+\\mathrm{CN}^{-}$\r\nBecause $\\mathrm{PO}_{4}^{3-}$ has highest charge among the given anions, therefore, $\\mathrm{Mg}_{3}\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_{4}\\right)_{2}$ is the most effective in the coagulation of $\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_{3}$ solution.",
            "image": null
          },
